      "side": 1,
      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] Because `EC_CMD_FP_TEMPLATE` handles both V0 and V1 packets and registers using `SMALLEST_TYPE(struct ec_params_fp_template, struct ec_params_fp_template_v1)`, the framework only guarantees `args-\u003einput_buf_size \u003e\u003d 8`. \n\nHowever, `params-\u003ecmd` is at offset 8 (the 9th byte) in `struct ec_params_fp_template_v1`. If a V1 packet of size 8 is received, reading `params-\u003ecmd` here will result in an out-of-bounds read.\n\nPlease add an explicit size check for the V1 structure before accessing `params-\u003ecmd`:\n\n```cpp\nstatic enum ec_host_cmd_status\nfp_command_template_v1(struct ec_host_cmd_handler_args *args)\n{\n\tif (args-\u003einput_buf_size \u003c offsetof(struct ec_params_fp_template_v1, data)) {\n\t\treturn EC_HOST_CMD_INVALID_PARAM;\n\t}\n\n\tconst auto *params \u003d\n\t\tstatic_cast\u003cconst struct ec_params_fp_template_v1 *\u003e(\n\t\t\targs-\u003einput_buf);\n\tenum ec_status status;\n\n\tswitch (params-\u003ecmd) {\n```\n[🔗](http://go/tj/cns/gg-d/home/tomhughes@google.com/review_trajectories/cl8464410_49822016-13d9-4f58-9e86-1a7b5f08dbee.pb)",
